{"id": "EUVD-2026-76437", "enisaUuid": "98d4a695-9c92-39b3-b544-33da56b9b90f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsvcrdma: Reject connection when transport allocation fails\n\nhandle_connect_req() returns without action when\nsvc_rdma_create_xprt() fails to allocate the new transport.\nThe CM core returns 0 for CONNECT_REQUEST events, so it does\nnot destroy the new rdma_cm_id. Each allocation failure under\nmemory pressure leaks one rdma_cm_id, and a remote peer driving\nconnection attempts can amplify this.\n\nReject the connection by returning a non-zero status from the\nCM event handler, which tells the CM core to destroy the\norphaned cm_id.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:47:43", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5bf47bbea3c22c0af2293b6c393ab04d5420f7ab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e21754bbf75075f3fee1cebc79f3417364235ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3cf372cec7ab2cd8c6002bf775cc14d90ccb098b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1f6a14c142fee4778c32709d1d54595c2e2b7991", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0944462247dcb7de7622cdaaadf5f05c52707dab"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vgrv-wfr9-vqh2", "CVE-2026-89531"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1fb0f4e2-b116-36f4-b17d-a967390d8f31", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.25"}, {"id": "3142bb71-c685-3b02-9632-8670c155a209", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "3a167e46-d15d-3e01-8061-409a7887118e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "41d6fe8b-d112-35f3-a954-ced560f5f94d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "528d32c7-2542-38d7-9046-eef294d54da9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "377f9b2f4529e0ac702fd7b91e216afd0adc959e <6e21754bbf75075f3fee1cebc79f3417364235ec"}, {"id": "643e2be7-2a42-3a3c-88d0-d23f7160e7bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "377f9b2f4529e0ac702fd7b91e216afd0adc959e <5bf47bbea3c22c0af2293b6c393ab04d5420f7ab"}, {"id": "66777ce3-1298-3ff2-8d8b-0e49f44978a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "67f9c95a-bafc-3300-886d-b7f567956cc7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "377f9b2f4529e0ac702fd7b91e216afd0adc959e <0944462247dcb7de7622cdaaadf5f05c52707dab"}, {"id": "6df791a9-dad7-3573-aa12-6ef5a5be6778", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "dee9b4d2-d4a9-3b4d-808a-356cc9dd714a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "377f9b2f4529e0ac702fd7b91e216afd0adc959e <1f6a14c142fee4778c32709d1d54595c2e2b7991"}, {"id": "f33f132a-ad6c-3f49-ae17-518af79d3dc2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "377f9b2f4529e0ac702fd7b91e216afd0adc959e <3cf372cec7ab2cd8c6002bf775cc14d90ccb098b"}, {"id": "f9557fa4-8d15-33ca-8294-302ab61eed3d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ee8e75ef-9e6d-324a-9b53-9de619382427", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}